WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.820
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.745 --> 00:00:07.370
SPEAKER 1: Give me
one minute, and I'll

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:10.520
show you how local SSD can
add some extra storage space

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.170
for your virtual machines.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:14.740
Local SSD is local
solid state drive

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.910
storage for your VM instances.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:19.910
It provides the lowest latency
and highest performance storage

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.260
for temporary use cases.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.830
Local SSDs are physically
attached to the server that

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:28.670
hosts your VM instance, giving
you superior performance, very

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:32.119
high input/output operations per
second, and very low latency,

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:34.880
compared to other
block storage options.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.280
You can customize the VM
shape to your workload,

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.020
or attach predefined
shapes designed

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.920
for typical use cases, like
data analytics, media rendering,

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:44.570
or gaming.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:46.760
Your data is secure
because it's encrypted

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:49.610
with an ephemeral encryption
key that's managed and protected

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:51.380
by the SSD.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:54.950
Local SSDs can be created only
during the instance creation

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.090
process.

00:00:56.090 --> 00:01:01.100
After creating a local SSD,
format and mount the device.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.830
Local SSDs are designed
for temporary storage use

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:07.440
cases, such as caches or
scratch processing space,

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.860
which makes them suitable
for workloads, like media

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:13.800
rendering, data analytics, or
high performance computing.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.670
So next time you're thinking
about adding ephemeral storage

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:20.120
to your VM, take a minute
and look at local SSD.

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:22.490
For more info on
local SSD, check out

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:26.330
cloud.google.com/local-ssd.

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:29.680
[MUSIC PLAYING]

